# Array-Driven Race Fetch

Queries all CDN endpoints simultaneously. The fastest successful response resolves the request, while slower pending requests are instantly aborted via `AbortController`.

**Benefits:**
- Minimizes latency
- Improves reliability across geographic regions
- Automatic failover

**Implementation:**
```js
// Internal mechanism
const controllers = []
const promises = endpoints.map((url, i) => {
  const controller = new AbortController()
  controllers.push(controller)
  return fetch(url, { signal: controller.signal })
})
const response = await Promise.race(promises)
// Abort all other pending requests
controllers.forEach(c => c.abort())
```

# Dynamic Game Loading

Example of dynamically changing games by updating the `alias` attribute.

## JavaScript
```js
// Get the game element
const gameEl = document.querySelector('nex-game')

// Load a different game
gameEl.setAttribute('alias', 'bloxorz')

// The component automatically:
// 1. Terminates active streams
// 2. Clears event registries
// 3. Hot-reloads the new game
```

## HTML
```html
<nex-game id="game-container" alias="fnaf" gid="dynamic-1"></nex-game>

<button onclick="loadGame('bloxorz')">Play Bloxorz</button>
<button onclick="loadGame('2048')">Play 2048</button>

<script>
function loadGame(alias) {
  document.getElementById('game-container').setAttribute('alias', alias)
}
</script>
```
